@expand_aid_afganistan
title: Expand aid to the Afgani army
subtitle: This could help delay the collapse of the Afgani army
view-if: afganistan_fall = 0 and afgan_withdraw_month > 1
on-arrival: economic_democracy += 1; workers_spd += 7*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; works_councils += 1; new_liberal_dissent -= 6; new_liberal_strength += 8; dvp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent +=1 if in_grand_coalition
max-visits: 1

The works councils, elected by workers at each major business, have been in place since the German Revolution of 1918, but they have been largely powerless in the face of capital. Now, we will have worker representation on the boards of companies, giving them more influence in management decisions.



